+
+## Character Swap replacements
+
+Version 6 workers use `video_character_swap.py` for replace edits before the
+Viggle/H3 fallback. The approved primary Character Swap and Ref2VA DMD LoRAs run
+at strength 1 with eight Euler/simple steps, CFG 1 and sigma shifts 12/3. Native
+H3 image-reference conditioning supplies the replacement, while Add Guide receives
+the original shot frames. Add edits stay on the existing Fun ControlNet path.
+
+The renderer keeps the source aspect within a 0.5 MP canvas, splits at detected
+cuts and limits windows to 124 frames. It pads short windows and trims them back
+before restoring the original soundtrack. It does not repaint a still, composite
+SAM masks, generate audio or run a lip-sync post-pass. This matches the approved
+local comparisons; wider framing, background changes and seams between independent
+windows remain possible. Selection of one subject or a group follows the broker's
+grounded target in the prompt.
+
+`edited.character-swap.json` records segment graphs, timings and failures.
+Missing models, render errors and empty output fall back to Viggle/H3; cancelling
+stops without fallback. Set `VIDEO_EDIT_CHARACTER_SWAP=0` in the worker environment
+and reload the idle worker to roll back. `VIDEO_EDIT_REPAINT=0` on the broker only
+controls repainting in the legacy fallback.
+
+The deployment operator confirmed author permission for remote use of the Character
+Swap weights. Other installations need their own applicable permission under the
+BFS Character Swap license. The repository's `desktop/video-character-swap-models.json`
+records exact weight revisions and SHA-256 hashes. Install code using
+`scripts/apply-video-character-swap-desktop.py` from the bot repository.
